          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em differential categories
            (
            %a{:href => "#BluteCocketSeely06"} Blute, Cocket &amp; Seely 2006
            is meant to provide
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorical+semantics"} categorical semantics
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+linear+logic"} differential linear logic
            (
            %a{:href => "#EhrhardtRegnier09"}> Ehrhardt &amp; Regnier 2009
            ) which in turn is meant to be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/syntax"} syntactic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proof+theory"} proof-theoretic
            approach to
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+calculus"} differential calculus
          %h2#DifferentialCategories Differential categories
          %p
            The main intuition for differential categories, is that in a differential category morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \rightarrow B
            must be interpreted as linear morphisms from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            while morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo !
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !A \rightarrow B
            must be interpreted as smooth morphisms from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mo !
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f:!A \rightarrow B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo !
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(f):!A \otimes A \rightarrow B
            which is smooth in the first variable and linear in the second variable. If we are in a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+closed+category"} monoidal closed category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D(f)
            as a morphisms of type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo !
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo ⊸
                  %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} !A \rightarrow (A \multimap B)
            which associate smoothly to every point of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            the linear approximation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            around this point.
          %p
          .num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A coalgebra modality in a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝒞
                    %mo ,
